cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this engine or its benchmark, please cite it as below. Quote the held-out figures (docs/EVALUATION.md), not the in-sample ones."
title: "Rule-based grapheme-to-phoneme engine for Irish (Connacht, Munster, Ulster)"
type: software
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-23"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hellpanderrr/IrishPhoneticTranscription"
url: "https://hellpanderrr.github.io/wiktionary_pron/?lang=Irish"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A Lua engine that converts Irish spelling to IPA for three dialects, as a 17-pass pipeline over a token
  array plus a per-word exception layer. Runs under Lua 5.4 and in the browser (wasmoon). The repository
  includes a benchmark built from English Wiktionary pronunciations with a fixed train/test split.
keywords:
  - Irish
  - Gaeilge
  - grapheme-to-phoneme
  - IPA
  - phonetic transcription
authors:
  - alias: hellpanderrr   # replace with family-names / given-names (and orcid, optional)
references:
  - type: book
    title: "The Sound Structure of Modern Irish"
    authors:
      - family-names: Hickey
        given-names: Raymond
    publisher:
      name: "De Gruyter Mouton"
    year: 2014
  - type: book
    title: "Fuaimeanna na Gaeilge"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Ó Raghallaigh"
        given-names: Brian
    publisher:
      name: "Cois Life"
    year: 2013
  - type: data
    title: "English Wiktionary, Irish pronunciation entries"
    authors:
      - name: "Wiktionary contributors"
    url: "https://en.wiktionary.org"
    license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
  - type: software
    title: "ustring (Scribunto)"
    authors:
      - family-names: Jorsch
        given-names: Brad
    license: MIT
